{
  "raw": {
    "https://www.buzzfeed.com/jobs?edition=us": {
      "title": "Join our team",
      "description": "Jobs at BuzzFeed About Press Jobs Contact Investors Legal Join our team At BuzzFeed Inc., we’ve created an environment where employees can bring their authentic selves to work while building tools and creating content that spreads joy and truth, and helps connect people across the globe. See Openings Diversity, Inclusion, and Belonging At BuzzFeed Inc., it's important to us that our employees reflect the diversity in the world around us and that we cultivate an environment where everyone feels empowered to be their authentic self. Much of the work being done to create this environment is through our Employee Resource Groups. Our ERGs lead company-wide events and engagements that help to cultivate an environment that enables all employees to show up authentically. Employee Resource Groups at BuzzFeed Inc. BuzzFeed Inc. currently has 6 ERGs with chapters in several BuzzFeed office locations. Our ERGs work hard to create affinity communities, celebrate heritage months and generate awareness around important issues impacting BuzzFeeders. Perks & Benefits As a BuzzFeed Inc. employee, you will enjoy perks like company-wide events, career development courses, and no work on your birthday! But most importantly, you’ll work alongside inspiring colleagues to build tools and create content that connects hundreds of millions of people and brings truth and joy to people all over the world. Come join us! Wellness Comprehensive benefits for medical, dental, and vision insurance with a focus on Wellness. Plus discounts on Gyms, Care.com , and access to resources like Maven, Headspace Care, and One Medical. Planning for the future Take advantage of the 401(k) plan with a company match, and supplemental life insurance options. Work-life balance We offer our employees paid time off (including your birthday!), paid holidays and generous leave options for life events such as becoming a parent or getting married. Career development Opportunities for personal and professional growth via work experience, offerings from our in-house Learning @ BuzzFeed team, our Employee Resource Groups, and more. Our Interview Process You’re about to embark on an adventure to join one of BuzzFeed Inc.’s dynamic teams. Here’s your roadmap to becoming part of our story: Workplace Awards BuzzFeed is a winner of Digiday's Work Life Award for Most Innovative Culture. In 2019, BuzzFeed was named one of the Best Places to Work for LGBTQ Equality by HRC’s Corporate Equality Index . People of BuzzFeed Find us on Instagram @peopleofbuzzfeed All job applications must be received through the official BuzzFeed Inc. Jobs board ( https://www.buzzfeed.com/about/jobs ), including referrals. It is BuzzFeed Inc.'s practice to not schedule job interviews until after an application is submitted through our jobs board. BuzzFeed Inc. is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to, and will not be discriminated against based on age, race, gender, color, religion, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity, veteran status, disability or any other protected category. EEO is the law"
    },
    "https://boards.greenhouse.io/buzzfeed/jobs/8175418?gh_jid=8175418": {
      "title": "Account Manager",
      "description": "Job Application for Account Manager at Employment Opportunities at BuzzFeed, Inc. Back to jobs New Account Manager New York Apply About BuzzFeed, Inc. BuzzFeed, Inc. (Nasdaq: BZFD) is home to the best of the internet with a mission to spread joy and truth. Across entertainment, news, food, pop culture, and commerce, our brands drive conversation and inspire what audiences watch, read, and buy now — and into the future. Born on the internet in 2006, BuzzFeed, Inc. is committed to improving it: providing trusted, quality, brand-safe entertainment to hundreds of millions of people; making content on the internet more inclusive, empathetic, and creative; and inspiring our audience to live better lives. Salary: $51,000.00 - $77,000.00 USD BuzzFeed is looking for a detailed customer-service-focused individual to help manage BuzzFeed's advertising operations. As the Account Manager, you will lead the creation of strategic sales proposals and work with internal teams to develop ideas and concepts to solve client goals that are rooted in storytelling and insights. You will be your client's primary contact for campaign execution to ensure the success of the program and help promote renewals. You Will: Partner with Sales in building successful client and agency relationships, growing the partnership and in selling through BuzzFeed solutions and strategy Hold a general knowledge of all aspects of industry and clients' business and the ability to apply that knowledge to meaningful insights, counsel and planning for your client's business and BuzzFeed assignments Build proposal decks and create media plans in response to RFPs (Request For Proposal) Enter and manage insertion orders (IOs) within third-party and internal sales operations systems and support the billing team during month-end close Be your client’s primary contact for the program in relation to campaign execution, performance, and upsells via kick off calls, wrap up/recap presentations and day-to-day correspondence Facilitate internal communication between sales and other functions within the advertising org Partner with Creative, Production, Distribution and other teams to successfully launch and manage programs and production schedules Report to our Senior Manager of Account Management You Have: 2+ years experience working at a publisher, media or creative agency managing a brand's digital advertising strategy, creative development and buying activities Experience partnering with internal teams to brainstorm solutions that achieve client goals and future needs Experience in a client-facing role and comfortable presenting to different audiences, tailoring messages accordingly Worked on complex programs across a variety of spend levels and markets Experience monitoring and reporting on program performance and delivery by working with distribution and advertising operations teams Project management experience and ability to navigate and communicate deliverables with accuracy Experience and ability to tell a story using data, research and insights Google Product Suite, Powerpoint, Excel, Basecamp, Slack and Boostr knowledge a plus Life at BuzzFeed, Inc. We celebrate inclusion and are committed to equal-opportunity employment. We are proud to be an equal-opportunity workplace. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to, and will not be discriminated against based on age, race, gender, color, religion, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity, veteran status, disability, or any other protected category. You can expect: A supportive, inclusive atmosphere on a team that values your contributions. Opportunities for personal and professional growth through work experience, our Employee Resource Groups, and more. An attractive and equitable compensation package, including salary. A well-rounded benefits program featuring paid time off, unlimited sick time, comprehensive medical benefits, a family leave policy, access to mental health platforms, retirement plans, health and wellness discounts, and much more. Apply for this job * indicates a required field First Name * Last Name * Preferred First Name Email * Phone Country * Phone * Location (City) * Locate me Resume/CV * Attach Attach Dropbox Google Drive Enter manually Enter manually Accepted file types: pdf, doc, docx, txt, rtf Cover Letter Attach Attach Dropbox Google Drive Enter manually Enter manually Accepted file types: pdf, doc, docx, txt, rtf Education School Select... Degree Select... Discipline Select... Start date year End date year Add another LinkedIn Profile Website/Links to Samples or Portfolio Preferred pronoun (She/Her; He/His; They/Their; etc...) How did you hear about this job? * What is your desired salary for this position? * Are you legally authorized to work for any employer in the United States without any restrictions? * Select... Will you now or in the future require sponsorship to maintain that work authorization (e.g., H-1B status)? Note: Responding “Yes” to this question will not preclude you from consideration for employment. Select... Point of Data Transfer Select... BuzzFeed is committed to providing a welcoming and inclusive work environment, starting from our application process. From our annual diversity report to our Employee Resource Groups, we make diversity a centerpiece of our hiring practices and employee experience. Part of that is allowing candidates to voluntarily complete the following survey that assists in our efforts to ensure equal employment opportunities globally. Buzzfeed is required to ask some of the questions below under applicable law in certain jurisdictions, and we include the information we receive in anonymized, aggregated mandatory reporting.  We ask additional questions because we believe it will assist us in improving our diversity, inclusion, and belonging initiatives.  However, you are not required to answer any of the questions in order to submit and have your application considered by us.  If you choose to answer these questions, you are providing this information only for the uses described here, and not for any other purpose. Information collected as part of this survey : is voluntary; is anonymous; is not tied to your individual application; and does not have any bearing on your application; we will not know if you complete this survey or not; is used in aggregate form only, for use in anonymized reporting related to our diversity and inclusion efforts. This information will be stored in Greenhouse (you can review Greenhouse’s privacy policy here ).  Access inside BuzzFeed to this information is restricted to the People team.  Greenhouse will retain this information, along with the rest of the information provided in your application, 18 months from your application date, after which all application information will be anonymized and stored only in that form.  Once information is anonymized, neither we nor Greenhouse can determine the individual to whom it once belonged. Please select “Acknowledge” to indicate that you agree to our processing of this information for this purpose (if you do not wish to agree, do not complete the questions) Voluntary Identification Survey BuzzFeed Media Enterprises is committed to providing a welcoming and inclusive work environment, starting from our application process. From our annual diversity report to our Employee Resource Groups, we make diversity a centerpiece of our hiring practices and employee experience. Part of that is allowing candidates to voluntarily complete the following survey that assists in our efforts to ensure equal employment opportunities globally. Information collected as part of this survey : is voluntary; is anonymous; is not tied to your individual application; and does not have any bearing on your application; we will not know if you complete this survey or not; is collected in aggregate only, for use in anonymized reporting related to our diversity and inclusion efforts. I identify my gender as Select... I identify my race as Select... I identify my sexual orientation as Select... Veteran Status Select... Disability Status Select... Voluntary Self-Identification For government reporting purposes, we ask candidates to respond to the below self-identification survey.\nCompletion of the form is entirely voluntary. Whatever your decision, it will not be considered in the hiring\nprocess or thereafter. Any information that you do provide will be recorded and maintained in a\nconfidential file. As set forth in Employment Opportunities at BuzzFeed, Inc.’s Equal Employment Opportunity policy,\nwe do not discriminate on the basis of any protected group status under any applicable law. Gender Select... Are you Hispanic/Latino? Select... Race & Ethnicity Definitions If you believe you belong to any of the categories of protected veterans listed below, please indicate by making the appropriate selection.\n  As a government contractor subject to the Vietnam Era Veterans Readjustment Assistance Act (VEVRAA), we request this information in order to measure\n  the effectiveness of the outreach and positive recruitment efforts we undertake pursuant to VEVRAA. Classification of protected categories\n  is as follows: A \"disabled veteran\" is one of the following: a veteran of the U.S. military, ground, naval or air service who is entitled to compensation (or who but for the receipt of military retired pay would be entitled to compensation) under laws administered by the Secretary of Veterans Affairs; or a person who was discharged or released from active duty because of a service-connected disability. A \"recently separated veteran\" means any veteran during the three-year period beginning on the date of such veteran's discharge or release from active duty in the U.S. military, ground, naval, or air service. An \"active duty wartime or campaign badge veteran\" means a veteran who served on active duty in the U.S. military, ground, naval or air service during a war, or in a campaign or expedition for which a campaign badge has been authorized under the laws administered by the Department of Defense. An \"Armed forces service medal veteran\" means a veteran who, while serving on active duty in the U.S. military, ground, naval or air service, participated in a United States military operation for which an Armed Forces service medal was awarded pursuant to Executive Order 12985. Veteran Status Select... Voluntary Self-Identification of Disability Form CC-305 Page 1 of 1 OMB Control Number 1250-0005 Expires 07/31/2029 Why are you being asked to complete this form? We are a federal contractor or subcontractor. The law requires us to provide equal employment opportunity to qualified people with disabilities. We have a goal of having at least 7% of our workers as people with disabilities. The law says we must measure our progress towards this goal. To do this, we must ask applicants and employees if they have a disability or have ever had one. People can become disabled, so we need to ask this question at least every five years. Completing this form is voluntary, and we hope that you will choose to do so. Your answer is confidential. No one who makes hiring decisions will see it. Your decision to complete the form and your answer will not harm you in any way. If you want to learn more about the law or this form, visit the U.S. Department of Labor’s Office of Federal Contract Compliance Programs (OFCCP) website at www.dol.gov/ofccp . How do you know if you have a disability? A disability is a condition that substantially limits one or more of your “major life activities.” If you have or have ever had such a condition, you are a person with a disability. Disabilities include, but are not limited to: Alcohol or other substance use disorder (not currently using drugs illegally) Autoimmune disorder, for example, lupus, fibromyalgia, rheumatoid arthritis, HIV/AIDS Blind or low vision Cancer (past or present) Cardiovascular or heart disease Celiac disease Cerebral palsy Deaf or serious difficulty hearing Diabetes Disfigurement, for example, disfigurement caused by burns, wounds, accidents, or congenital disorders Epilepsy or other seizure disorder Gastrointestinal disorders, for example, Crohn's Disease, irritable bowel syndrome Intellectual or developmental disability Mental health conditions, for example, depression, bipolar disorder, anxiety disorder, schizophrenia, PTSD Missing limbs or partially missing limbs Mobility impairment, benefiting from the use of a wheelchair, scooter, walker, leg brace(s) and/or other supports Nervous system condition, for example, migraine headaches, Parkinson’s disease, multiple sclerosis (MS) Neurodivergence, for example, attention-deficit/hyperactivity disorder (ADHD), autism spectrum disorder, dyslexia, dyspraxia, other learning disabilities Partial or complete paralysis (any cause) Pulmonary or respiratory conditions, for example, tuberculosis, asthma, emphysema Short stature (dwarfism) Traumatic brain injury Disability Status Select... PUBLIC BURDEN STATEMENT: According to the Paperwork Reduction Act of 1995 no persons are required to respond to a collection of information unless such collection displays a valid OMB control number. This survey should take about 5 minutes to complete. Submit application Powered by Greenhouse"
    },
    "https://boards.greenhouse.io/buzzfeed/jobs/8155125?gh_jid=8155125": {
      "title": "Content Writer (Project-Based)",
      "description": "Job Application for Content Writer (Project-Based) at Employment Opportunities at BuzzFeed, Inc. Back to jobs Content Writer (Project-Based) India-Remote Apply About BuzzFeed, Inc. BuzzFeed, Inc. (Ticker: BZFD) is home to the best of the internet. Across food, news, pop culture, and commerce, our brands drive conversation and inspire what audiences watch, read, buy, and obsess over next. Born on the internet in 2006, BuzzFeed, Inc. is committed to improving it: providing trusted, quality, brand-safe news and entertainment to hundreds of millions of people; making content on the internet more inclusive, empathetic, and creative; and inspiring our audience to live better lives. We'll continue to recruit the best founders and creators to join us in this mission, with more additions like HuffPost to come. Applicants for this role must be based in India. Business Area: Content Job Category: Content Monthly: 45,000 per month INR Union Status: Non-Union BuzzFeed Inc. is committed to fair and equitable compensation practices. We reserve the ability to adjust the final compensation for this role based on the final candidate's experience, skillset, certifications, and geography. The Role Are you obsessed with internet culture? Do you love turning trending moments into something people can’t stop reading about? BuzzFeed’s India team is looking for curious, internet-savvy writers to craft engaging, entertaining, and shareable stories for our US audience. If you have a keen eye for pop culture moments, a sharp sense of humor, and know how to make people click , this role is for you. What you'll do Pitch and write engaging listicles, quizzes, and feature stories across pop culture, entertainment, and lifestyle, centred around the US audience. Turn trending conversations and niche topics into compelling, high-performing content. Work with the editor to refine content, optimize headlines, and package stories for maximum impact. Take ownership of your ideas from pitch to publication and iterate based on editorial feedback and performance. Spot great stories before everyone else does. What we're looking for Applicants for this role must be based in India. A creative and versatile writer with 1–3 years of experience in content, editorial, or journalism. Bonus points if you have previously worked with a digital content company. Freshers who show promise with exceptional creative skills will also be considered. Excellent written English and a strong grasp of grammar. A genuine curiosity about internet culture, pop culture, and why people share content. Strong research skills and attention to detail. Ability to think like a reader and package stories with compelling headlines and hooks. Organized, deadline-driven, and able to juggle multiple stories at once. Someone who takes initiative, works independently, and is eager to learn from data and feedback. Comfortable with CMS tools. This is a full-time 40-hour-a-week contract position, Monday through Friday, with the ability to work remotely as long as you are based in India . Contracts are 3 months to start with the potential opportunity to extend to a year. If you think this is you, please submit your materials below AND fill out this Google Form . Both components are required for a complete submission. We'll be in touch if it's a fit! Apply for this job * indicates a required field First Name * Last Name * Email * Phone Country * Phone * Resume/CV * Attach Attach Dropbox Google Drive Enter manually Enter manually Accepted file types: pdf, doc, docx, txt, rtf Cover Letter Attach Attach Dropbox Google Drive Enter manually Enter manually Accepted file types: pdf, doc, docx, txt, rtf Pronouns (She/Her; He/His; They/Them; etc...) * How did you hear about this job? * Will you now or in the future require sponsorship to maintain that work authorization (e.g., H-1B status)? Note: Responding “Yes” to this question will not preclude you from consideration for employment. * Select... Point of Data Transfer * Select... BuzzFeed is committed to providing a welcoming and inclusive work environment, starting from our application process. From our annual diversity report to our Employee Resource Groups, we make diversity a centerpiece of our hiring practices and employee experience. Part of that is allowing candidates to voluntarily complete the following survey that assists in our efforts to ensure equal employment opportunities globally. Buzzfeed is required to ask some of the questions below under applicable law in certain jurisdictions, and we include the information we receive in anonymized, aggregated mandatory reporting.  We ask additional questions because we believe it will assist us in improving our diversity, inclusion, and belonging initiatives.  However, you are not required to answer any of the questions in order to submit and have your application considered by us.  If you choose to answer these questions, you are providing this information only for the uses described here, and not for any other purpose. Information collected as part of this survey : is voluntary; is anonymous; is not tied to your individual application; and does not have any bearing on your application; we will not know if you complete this survey or not; is used in aggregate form only, for use in anonymized reporting related to our diversity and inclusion efforts. This information will be stored in Greenhouse (you can review Greenhouse’s privacy policy here ).  Access inside BuzzFeed to this information is restricted to the People team.  Greenhouse will retain this information, along with the rest of the information provided in your application, 18 months from your application date, after which all application information will be anonymized and stored only in that form.  Once information is anonymized, neither we nor Greenhouse can determine the individual to whom it once belonged. Please select “Acknowledge” to indicate that you agree to our processing of this information for this purpose (if you do not wish to agree, do not complete the questions) Submit application Powered by Greenhouse"
    },
    "https://boards.greenhouse.io/buzzfeed/jobs/8160564?gh_jid=8160564": {
      "title": "Community Editor & Strategist (Project Based)",
      "description": "Job Application for Community Editor & Strategist (Project Based) at Employment Opportunities at BuzzFeed, Inc. Back to jobs Community Editor & Strategist (Project Based) Remote Apply Contract Community Editor & Strategist 3-month contract with potential to extend $25/hour, 40 hours a week Remote-friendly (LA or NYC office optional) BuzzFeed is seeking a Contract Community Editor & Strategist to join our dynamic team. This role blends editing, creator success, community management, and digital publishing strategy. You'll work closely with BuzzFeed's most passionate creators, helping them produce their best work while fostering an engaged, welcoming Community both on and off the site. This role is perfect for someone who loves internet culture, online communities, and helping creators succeed. About BuzzFeed Community BuzzFeed Community is a unique, user-powered corner of BuzzFeed.com where anyone can create an account and submit their own content — whether it’s listicles, quizzes, or personal essays. The platform is beloved by BuzzFeed’s most engaged users and often centers around fandoms, pop culture, and nostalgia. Community content is some of the most unique and fun content on our site, thanks to the passion and creativity of our users. Community posts are not only entertaining and engaging — they are a core part of BuzzFeed’s mission to amplify diverse voices and perspectives. What You'll Do As a Community Editor & Strategist, you'll help shape the future of BuzzFeed Community by editing high-quality user-generated content while building relationships with the creators behind it. You'll work closely with the Community Strategy team to grow our creator ecosystem and ensure contributors have the tools and feedback they need to thrive. You will: Edit submissions from the BuzzFeed Community Creator Program (BFCCP) , ensuring they meet BuzzFeed's editorial standards for quality, accuracy, and style. Partner directly with Community Creators by providing thoughtful editorial feedback, coaching, and best practices to help them improve their content over time. Foster an active, welcoming creator community by engaging with contributors in our Discord server, answering questions, encouraging participation, and building relationships. Moderate Community content and comments to maintain a positive, inclusive environment. Curate standout Community content by identifying posts with strong editorial or viral potential. Use traffic and engagement data to inform editorial decisions and surface content that resonates with readers. Collaborate with BuzzFeed's Audience Development and Editorial teams on creator initiatives, publishing strategy, and special projects. Help identify opportunities to improve creator education, onboarding, and overall program success. You Have: A deep love for internet culture, fandom, and online communities. Excellent editing, grammar, and proofreading skills with exceptional attention to detail. Strong written communication skills and the ability to deliver thoughtful, constructive feedback to creators. Experience building relationships with online communities or creators. An understanding of what makes BuzzFeed-style content engaging and shareable. Strong organizational skills and the ability to manage multiple priorities in a fast-paced environment. Comfort working independently while collaborating across editorial and audience teams. Familiarity with CMS platforms and digital publishing workflows. Interest in audience development, analytics, SEO, and social strategy is a plus. Bonus Points For: Previous experience editing user-generated or creator-produced content. Experience managing online communities, including Discord servers, forums, or creator programs. Experience with social media community management, including responding to comments and engaging audiences across platforms like Facebook, Instagram, TikTok, or Twitter/X. Experience working with creators or influencers. If you're excited about fostering creativity, empowering users, and shaping viral internet content, we’d love to hear from you! Apply for this job * indicates a required field First Name * Last Name * Email * Phone Country * Phone * Resume/CV * Attach Attach Dropbox Google Drive Enter manually Enter manually Accepted file types: pdf, doc, docx, txt, rtf Cover Letter Attach Attach Dropbox Google Drive Enter manually Enter manually Accepted file types: pdf, doc, docx, txt, rtf LinkedIn Profile Website/Links to Samples or Portfolio * Link your BuzzFeed Community profile (with the requested information added) here. Pronouns (She/Her; He/His; They/Them; etc...) How did you hear about this job? * What is your desired salary for this position? * Are you legally authorized to work for any employer in the United States without any restrictions? * Select... Will you now or in the future require sponsorship to maintain that work authorization (e.g., H-1B status)? Note: Responding “Yes” to this question will not preclude you from consideration for employment. Select... Point of Data Transfer Select... BuzzFeed is committed to providing a welcoming and inclusive work environment, starting from our application process. From our annual diversity report to our Employee Resource Groups, we make diversity a centerpiece of our hiring practices and employee experience. Part of that is allowing candidates to voluntarily complete the following survey that assists in our efforts to ensure equal employment opportunities globally. Buzzfeed is required to ask some of the questions below under applicable law in certain jurisdictions, and we include the information we receive in anonymized, aggregated mandatory reporting.  We ask additional questions because we believe it will assist us in improving our diversity, inclusion, and belonging initiatives.  However, you are not required to answer any of the questions in order to submit and have your application considered by us.  If you choose to answer these 